//
//  Gathering stage 3, part "Resource storage": the storage events of the retail harvests and kills that fill the pawn's Resource containers (tests/capture_resource.h, generated by
//  tools/capture/gen_resource.py from 22 captures) against the typed codecs of protocol/repl.
//
//    * the 24 events (18 into Resource0, 6 into Resource1) without the optional "Acquired <item>" text read to their last bit, typed: one target container with one slot, the count of
//      the item's quantity, status 14 ("no error"), no move source, Type Add, and are written back to the exact bits
//    * the target's shape: its distance from the Equipment container is 8 (Resource0) or 10 (Resource1), the slot is inside the grid of any bag (below 40), the target's slot guid is the
//      event's item guid; the item has a record, a quantity from 1 to 99 and a quality from 1 to 200; the 24 instance guids are all different
//    * the event as captured is longer by the callout only: full_bits = bits + toast_bits, the callout is about 5.3 kbit
//    * the same events built from what they say (record, quantity, quality, guid, slot, container) by storage_event_params equal the capture's bits, so a harvest's Add that worldd sends
//      is the retail one up to the callout
//    * the 24 events AS CAPTURED (Gathering stage 3, "the pick-up popup"): the optional struct is a TOptional<FCalloutQueueInfo> that the codec reads to the last bit and writes back to
//      the exact bits: the message "Acquired <a ...> [Name] </>xN" (and its copy), the item again, the callout's type 6, point size 36 and chat category 141, nothing else but the time;
//      without the callout the event is the toastless one above
// ============================================================================
